        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "109bc406-03e1-5a4b-a74a-0bf992553dd7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Madeleine (1950 film)\n- People: David Lean, Madeleine Smith, Emile L'Angelier, Ann Todd, Dorothy Anne Todd\n- Places: Glasgow\n- Events: Madeleine Smith murder trial\n- Topics: true-story adaptation, media publicity\n\nFacts:\n- In 1857, Madeleine Smith, a young woman from a wealthy Glasgow family, was tried for the murder of her lover, Emile L'Angelier.\n- The Madeleine Smith trial was heavily publicized in newspapers at the time and was labeled \"the trial of the century.\"\n- In 1950, the film Madeleine was directed by David Lean and was based on the true story of Madeleine Smith.\n- Dorothy Anne Todd, known as Ann Todd, was born on 24 January 1909 and was an English actress and producer.\n- Ann Todd died on 6 May 1993.",
